NEARS-3007 AC1 FAIL — evidence log

1) BrandsViewWidget (the ONLY code path to BrandsScreen, via RouteHelper.getBrandsScreen())
   is mounted EXCLUSIVELY in UserApp/lib/features/home/screens/modules/shop_home_screen.dart
   (module_type == 'ecommerce'). grocery_home_screen.dart has ZERO brand references (grep
   confirmed empty match). So Home -> Grocery & Food module never shows a Brands carousel at
   all, regardless of DB content.

2) The only modules in this DB that mount shop_home_screen are the two ecommerce fixtures:
   module_id=9 "NEARS-2897 Shop (Ecommerce)" and module_id=10 "NEARS-2907 Campaign Banner
   Ecommerce" (both zone 1 / "Demo Zone — Dhaka").

3) BrandsRepository.getBrandList() sends the ACTIVE module's id as the `moduleId` header
   (Get.find<ModuleController>().module?.id). BrandController@get_brands (Admin) filters
   `Brand::Active()->where(whereNull('module_id') OR module_id = $headerModuleId)`.

4) Live app runtime log (this run, emulator-5558, zone 1 "Demo Zone — Dhaka",
   NEARS-2897 Shop (Ecommerce) module):
     I/flutter (24315): [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/brand
     I/flutter (24315): [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/brand http_status=200
   -> HTTP 200, but the Brands section never rendered on-screen (confirmed via
      uiautomator dump + ui_shot after scrolling shop_home_screen to its bottom —
      the last section is "Stores"/"Top Rated", no "Brands" header/See-all anywhere).

5) Direct endpoint reproduction (same backend, same DB) proves why:
     curl -s "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/brand" -H "zoneId: [1]" -H "moduleId: 9"
       -> []   (empty — module 9, the module actually active when BrandsViewWidget mounts)
     curl -s "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/brand" -H "zoneId: [1]" -H "moduleId: 10"
       -> []   (empty — module 10, same story)
     curl -s "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/brand" -H "zoneId: [1]" -H "moduleId: 1"
       -> [{"id":3,"name":"NEARS-3007 QA Brand", ..., "module_id":1, ...}]
          (the seeded brand — but module_id=1 is Grocery & Food, which never mounts
          BrandsViewWidget at all)

CONCLUSION: the seeded brand's module_id=1 (Grocery & Food) can never be reached through
BrandsViewWidget's only mount point (the ecommerce shop_home_screen, module_id 9/10). No
module_id currently active in the app's normal tap-through flow can both (a) render the
Brands carousel/"See all" AND (b) match a brand row with module_id=1. AC1 as specified
("Home -> tap See all on brands carousel -> land on BrandsScreen with the seeded brand
rendered, using ONLY normal in-app tap-through") is UNREACHABLE with the current seed data.
